-foreground/90 mb-6","children":"Ectoin is a small cyclic amino-acid derivative discovered in halophilic bacteria — organisms that survive in extreme salt concentrations, high temperatures and intense UV exposure. It is, in biochemical terms, an extremolyte: a molecule produced under stress to stabilise cells and proteins."}]}],["$","$L3","1",{"delay":0.03,"children":["$","p",null,{"className":"font-serif text-lg md:text-xl leading-[1.6] text-foreground/90 mb-6","children":"Applied to the skin, ectoin does something similar. It forms a stabilising shell of water around proteins and cellular structures, protecting them from environmental stressors — UV, pollution, heat, dryness — and visible irritation."}]}],["$","$L3","2",{"delay":0.06,"children":["$","p",null,{"className":"font-serif text-lg md:text-xl leading-[1.6] text-foreground/90 mb-6","children":"In clinical literature, ectoin has been shown to reduce the visible impact of UV-induced stress, improve hydration and reduce the appearance of redness. It is one of the rare actives that is genuinely multi-functional and well-tolerated across all skin types, including reactive."}]}],["$","$L3","3",{"delay":0.09,"children":["$","p",null,{"className":"font-serif text-lg md:text-xl leading-[1.6] text-foreground/90 mb-6","children":"We include ectoin in C15 Antioxidant Serum, Peptide Recovery Serum and Daily Mineral SPF 50. It is one of the reasons our formulations sit comfortably on stressed modern skin without stinging."}]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-border","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-muted-foreground font-mono uppercase tracking-wider","children":"AUREL is a fictional concept brand. Articles are educational demonstration content and do not constitute medical advice."}]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-bone-deep py-16 md:py-24","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-aurel","children":["$L5","$L6"]}]}],"$L7"]}]],["$L8"],"$L9"]}],"loading":nul